The program should explicitly seek answers to the following:

What constitutes an effective inpatient treatment environment?
Which interventions produce the greatest initial response?
Which interventions produce durable remission?
Does treatment sequencing materially affect outcome?
Does psychotherapy become more effective when delivered during specific pharmacological or psychological states?
Which patients benefit from which treatment pathways?
What are the best rescue strategies for nonresponders?
How long should structured inpatient care continue?
Does transitional housing materially improve long-term outcomes?
What duration of transitional housing is optimal?
Does employment accelerate recovery?
What role does transportation access play?
Which environmental factors predict relapse?
What treatment combinations produce synergistic effects?
What interventions produce benefits that persist after treatment ends?
What causes those benefits to persist?
What predicts relapse after initial remission?
Can relapse risk be detected early enough to permit adaptive intervention?
Which treatment trajectory produces the best cost-adjusted outcomes?
What is the societal cost of failing to provide effective treatment?
What is the cost of the optimal treatment trajectory?
